WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 001, en. Timings are estimates from the script until the clip is rendered.

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:13.846
<v Nia>Bore da. Gloves on before you touch anything. Before a single deed, we've got names. Just names, written in your family's research notes.

2
00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:22.658
<v The Grandson>Cedwyn. That's the word I keep tripping over. Cedwyn, Cwm-Cedwyn, Nant-Cedwyn, Ynys-Cedwyn. Then Cedfin, Cydfin, Cydwin. And Tŷ Mawr, the Great House.

3
00:00:23.008 --> 00:00:34.546
<v Nia>This is the index. Six research leads, GHF-E174 to GHF-E179. It shows where each name turns up, and which notes lean on which. Pull one out, you see what wobbles.

4
00:00:34.896 --> 00:00:41.435
<v The Grandson>So does it prove the farm was Cedwyn land? That we held it from some medieval manor?

5
00:00:41.785 --> 00:00:55.631
<v Nia>No. It proves we've catalogued the leads, nothing more. It doesn't show the variants are the same place, or that they mean Great House Farm, or that any old lease decides who owned what after 1877.

6
00:00:55.981 --> 00:01:02.904
<v The Grandson>Cwm-Cedwyn. A wooded dell on the Ely, between Leckwith and Llandough. My notes use it all the time.

7
00:01:03.254 --> 00:01:15.946
<v Nia>They do. But there's no source attached yet. We don't know when the name was first written, where its edges ran, or whether it ever touched the farm. Checking is still to do.

8
00:01:20.296 --> 00:01:24.142
<v The Grandson>And Nant-Cedwyn. A brook running into the Ely near Leckwith.

9
00:01:24.492 --> 00:01:39.877
<v Nia>That one points to a primary document, and we haven't got it. Not held. So for now it shows us nothing; only that the family noted the name. Name, place, date, link to Tŷ Mawr: all still to be checked.

10
00:01:40.227 --> 00:01:42.150
<v The Grandson>Ynys-Cedwyn's the odd one out.

11
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:51.731
<v Nia>Ynys-Cedwyn sits up where the Twrch meets the Tawe, a long way from here. The note ties it to Cedwyn Gawr, Cedwyn the Giant.

12
00:01:52.081 --> 00:01:55.927
<v The Grandson>A giant. Lovely. Is there anything linking him to Llandough?

13
00:01:56.277 --> 00:02:07.046
<v Nia>The note doesn't even try. No primary source, the place and the giant both waiting to be checked, and no connection to Great House Farm stated at all.

14
00:02:07.396 --> 00:02:11.627
<v The Grandson>So the film starts with a name we can't pin down.

15
00:02:11.977 --> 00:02:19.285
<v Nia>It starts honest. A name, and a hill that came before it. Let's go and stand on the hill.
